From 37c709496faafa3155d222bb211231c827d2171f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:32:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2504/3799] soh: rename func_800F45D0 ->
 Audio_PlayFishingReelSfx

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: drives NA_SE_IT_FISHING_REEL_SLOW on the interval timer with a rate-scaled companion sound
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_general.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_general.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_general.c b/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
index 51bdaa101..8cd930d9b 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
@@ -4512,7 +4512,8 @@ void Audio_PlaySfxWithVolume(Vec3f* pos, u16 sfxId, f32 arg2) {
     Audio_PlaySfxGeneral(sfxId, pos, 4, &gSfxDefaultFreqAndVolScale, &D_8016B7E0, &gSfxDefaultReverb);
 }
 
-void func_800F45D0(f32 arg0) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_800F45D0: drives NA_SE_IT_FISHING_REEL_SLOW on the interval timer with a rate-scaled companion sound
+void Audio_PlayFishingReelSfx(f32 arg0) {
     Audio_PlaySfxAtInterval(&gSfxDefaultPos, NA_SE_IT_FISHING_REEL_SLOW - SFX_FLAG, arg0);  // was func_800F4414 [LLM:HIGH]
     Audio_PlaySfxScaledByRate(&gSfxDefaultPos, 0, (0.15f * arg0) + 1.4f);  // was func_800F436C [LLM:HIGH]
 }
